    <string name="td_help_title">How to Play Tower Defence</string>
    <string name="td_help_text">Enemies attack from the left and march to your castle on the right. Each one that reaches the gate hurts the castle (a boss hurts it a lot). Hold out for all 10 waves.\n\nOn Castle Siege maps you can build anywhere that is buildable, even on the road. The only rule: enemies must always have a way to the gate, and the route may not become more than two and a half times longer. If a spot is refused, the game tells you why. Flyers ignore your maze.\n\nPick a tower at the bottom, then tap the field to see a ghost with a green check or a red cross, and tap it again to build. You can also press, drag and release. Tap a tower to upgrade, sell (75 percent back, all of it in the first 3 seconds), move or change what it targets. At level 3 choose one of two paths.\n\nBolt is fast and hits air. Blast splashes ground units. Control slows or stuns. Support boosts towers nearby. Brutes shrug off Bolt shots, so bring Blast.\n\nThe Classic maps keep their fixed tower spots. Gentle mode gives extra gold, softer waves and a sturdier castle.</string>
    <string name="td_leave_title">Leave this run?</string>
    <string name="td_leave_body_keep">This run is still in progress and will not count, but the runs you have already finished stay on your record.</string>
    <string name="td_leave_body">This run is still in progress. Leaving now will not count it as a win or a loss.</string>
    <string name="td_tip_1">Build anywhere you like, but always leave enemies a way to the gate.</string>
    <string name="td_tip_2">Brutes shrug off Bolt shots. Blast towers hurt them and anything near them.</string>
    <string name="td_tip_3">Tap a tower to change its targeting, upgrade it or sell it for most of its gold.</string>
